infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two window types: count-based vs time-based
  desc The failure rate is judged over a sliding window — both age out old calls, they differ in how recent is bounded
  compares
    - label Count-based — last N calls (resilience4j default)
      children
        - label Judges the last 100 calls
          desc resilience4j default: slidingWindowType COUNT_BASED, slidingWindowSize 100
        - label Simple and predictable
          desc The window is exactly N calls, easy to reason about
        - label Reacts slowly on quiet traffic
          desc On a low-traffic endpoint 100 calls can span a long time, so old failures linger
    - label Time-based — last T seconds in buckets (Hystrix)
      children
        - label Judges the last 10 s in buckets
          desc Hystrix: 10 s rolling window split into 10 one-second buckets, rolling each second
        - label Bounded wall-clock reaction
          desc Reacts within seconds regardless of traffic volume
        - label Best for latency-sensitive breakers
          desc What you usually want when a slow dependency is the danger
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
